---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  title={"Blood Pressure Log: BP Tracker Privacy Policy - PiFl Labs"}
  description={"PiFl Labs Co., Ltd. Blood Pressure Log: BP Tracker app privacy policy"}
  canonical="https://pifl-labs.com/en/apps/pipi-bp/privacy/"
  alternates={[{"hreflang":"en","href":"https://pifl-labs.com/en/apps/pipi-bp/privacy/"},{"hreflang":"ko","href":"https://pifl-labs.com/ko/apps/pipi-bp/privacy/"},{"hreflang":"ja","href":"https://pifl-labs.com/ja/apps/pipi-bp/privacy/"},{"hreflang":"x-default","href":"https://pifl-labs.com/ko/apps/pipi-bp/privacy/"}]}
  extraCss={["/styles.css"]}
>
<section class="legal-hero">
        <div class="container">
            <a href="/" class="legal-back"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Home</a>
            <h1><i class="fas fa-shield-alt"></i> <span class="text-gradient">Blood Pressure Log: BP Tracker Privacy Policy</span></h1>
            <p class="legal-date">Effective Date: October 25, 2026</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <main class="legal-page">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="legal-card">
                <p>PiFl Labs Co., Ltd. ("Company", "we", "us") is committed to protecting your personal data. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, store, and disclose information when you use the mobile application <strong>Blood Pressure Log: BP Tracker</strong> ("App"). For matters not covered here, our <a href="/privacy">general Privacy Policy</a> applies.</p>
                <p>The App does not measure blood pressure. It does not use any sensor, the camera, HealthKit, or Health Connect. You type in readings taken with your own home monitor.</p>

                <h2>1. Purpose of Processing</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>App functionality</strong>: Recording blood pressure and pulse readings, tags, notes, and reminder settings; reminders; exporting your records as PDF or CSV</li>
                    <li><strong>Advertising</strong>: Ad serving via Google AdMob</li>
                    <li><strong>Analytics</strong>: Anonymous usage statistics via Firebase Analytics (Google)</li>
                    <li><strong>Customer support</strong>: Receiving and responding to email inquiries</li>
                </ul>

                <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
                <p>The App does not require account registration. There is no cloud backup and no sync. We process the following:</p>
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Category</th>
                            <th>Items</th>
                            <th>Collection Method</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Health Records You Enter</td>
                            <td>Blood pressure readings, pulse, tags, notes, reminder settings</td>
                            <td>Stored only on your device in a local SQLite database (never transmitted to us or to any third party)</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Advertising Identifier</td>
                            <td>Ad ID (IDFA/AAID), coarse location (country level), device info (OS, model, language)</td>
                            <td>Automatic via Google AdMob SDK (with consent)</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Anonymous Usage Statistics</td>
                            <td>App opens, which features are used, counts and buckets (for example, the number of readings), standard Firebase identifiers (app instance ID), device info. Blood pressure values, categories, and notes are never collected.</td>
                            <td>Automatic via Firebase Analytics SDK (Google)</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Email Inquiries</td>
                            <td>Email address, name (optional), inquiry content</td>
                            <td>Direct email submission</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
                <p>Your health records are never used for ad targeting.</p>

                <h2>3. Retention Period</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Health records (local)</strong>: Until you delete individual readings in the App or delete the App. We hold no copy.</li>
                    <li><strong>Exported PDF/CSV files</strong>: Created on your device and shared only through your device's share sheet by your choice. We hold no copy; you manage these files.</li>
                    <li><strong>Advertising identifier and ad data</strong>: As per Google AdMob policy</li>
                    <li><strong>Anonymous usage statistics</strong>: As per Google Firebase policy</li>
                    <li><strong>Email inquiry records</strong>: <strong>3 years</strong> after resolution</li>
                </ul>

                <h2>4. Disclosure to Third Parties</h2>
                <p>We do not sell, trade, or transfer your personal information to third parties except as required by law or with your explicit consent. Your health records are stored only on your device and are never transmitted to us or to any third party.</p>

                <h2>5. Processing Entrustment</h2>
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Processor</th>
                            <th>Purpose</th>
                            <th>Retention</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Google LLC (AdMob)</td>
                            <td>Mobile ad serving and ad identifier processing</td>
                            <td>Until contract termination</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Google LLC (Firebase Analytics)</td>
                            <td>Anonymous usage statistics</td>
                            <td>Until contract termination</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>

                <h2>6. Advertising and Tracking Consent</h2>
                <p>The App shows banner ads, interstitial ads, and optional rewarded ads via Google AdMob. For this purpose AdMob may process advertising identifiers (IDFA/AAID), coarse location (country level), and device information. Your health records are never used for ad targeting.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>iOS users</strong>: The App asks for Apple's App Tracking Transparency (ATT) permission. <strong>If you decline, only non-personalized ads will be shown.</strong></li>
                    <li><strong>EEA and UK users</strong>: The Google User Messaging Platform (UMP) consent form is shown. You can change your choice at any time in Settings → Ad privacy options.</li>
                    <li><strong>Android users</strong>: You can opt out via Settings → Google → Ads → "Delete advertising ID" or "Opt out of ad personalization".</li>
                </ul>
                <p>For details on Google AdMob's data processing, see the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

                <h2>7. Analytics</h2>
                <p>The App uses Firebase Analytics (Google) to collect anonymous usage statistics, such as app opens, which features are used, and counts and buckets such as the number of readings. We never collect blood pressure values, categories, or notes. Google processes standard Firebase identifiers (app instance ID) and device information.</p>

                <h2>8. App Permissions</h2>
                <p>The App may request the following permissions. Each can be denied, though doing so may limit related functionality.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Notifications</strong>: Local reminders only. There is no push server.</li>
                    <li><strong>App Tracking Transparency (iOS)</strong>: Tracking consent for ad relevance</li>
                </ul>
                <p>The App does not use any sensor, the camera, HealthKit, or Health Connect.</p>

                <h2>9. In-App Purchases</h2>
                <p>Version 1.0 of the App has no in-app purchases. If this changes, we will update this Policy.</p>

                <h2>10. Data Destruction</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Procedure</strong>: Unnecessary personal data is destroyed after approval by the Data Protection Officer.</li>
                    <li><strong>Method</strong>: Electronic files are permanently deleted using non-recoverable methods. You can delete individual readings in the App. Local app data, including all your health records, is removed when you delete the App.</li>
                </ul>

                <h2>11. Your Rights</h2>
                <ol>
                    <li>Right to be informed about the processing of your personal data</li>
                    <li>Right to consent to and determine the scope of processing</li>
                    <li>Right to access and request information about your personal data</li>
                    <li>Right to request correction, deletion, suspension, or destruction</li>
                    <li>Right to seek redress for damages caused by processing</li>
                </ol>
                <p>To exercise these rights, contact us at <a href="#" data-email-user="privacy" data-email-domain="pifl-labs.com"><span class="email-text">privacy (at) pifl-labs.com</span></a>. Because your health records exist only on your device, you can delete individual readings directly in the App.</p>

                <h2>12. Security Measures</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li>Health records are stored only on your device and are never transmitted to us or to any third party</li>
                    <li>No account, no cloud backup, and no sync, so no copy of your health records is held on our servers</li>
                    <li>Exported files are shared only through your device's share sheet, by your choice</li>
                </ul>

                <h2>13. Children's Privacy</h2>
                <p>The App is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal data from children under 13. If we become aware of such collection, we will delete it immediately. Parents may request deletion at <a href="#" data-email-user="privacy" data-email-domain="pifl-labs.com"><span class="email-text">privacy (at) pifl-labs.com</span></a>.</p>

                <h2>14. International Data Transfers</h2>
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Recipient</th>
                            <th>Country</th>
                            <th>Purpose</th>
                            <th>Items</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Google LLC (AdMob)</td>
                            <td>United States</td>
                            <td>Mobile ad serving</td>
                            <td>Ad identifier, coarse location (country level), device info</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Google LLC (Firebase Analytics)</td>
                            <td>United States</td>
                            <td>Anonymous usage statistics</td>
                            <td>Usage events, app instance ID, device info</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>

                <h2>15. Data Protection Officer</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Company</strong>: PiFl Labs Co., Ltd.</li>
                    <li><strong>Email</strong>: <a href="#" data-email-user="privacy" data-email-domain="pifl-labs.com"><span class="email-text">privacy (at) pifl-labs.com</span></a></li>
                </ul>

                <h2>16. GDPR (European Economic Area)</h2>
                <p>If you are located in the EEA, you have additional rights under the General Data Protection Regulation, including the right to access, rectify, erase, restrict processing, data portability, and object to processing. Contact us at <a href="#" data-email-user="privacy" data-email-domain="pifl-labs.com"><span class="email-text">privacy (at) pifl-labs.com</span></a>.</p>

                <h2>17. Medical Disclaimer</h2>
                <p>The App is a personal record and does not provide medical advice. The categories shown in the App follow the American Heart Association 2017 ACC/AHA classification and are for reference only. Please consult a healthcare professional about your blood pressure and any treatment decisions.</p>

                <h2>18. Changes to this Policy</h2>
                <p>This Privacy Policy is effective as of October 25, 2026. Any changes will be announced on this page.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </main>
</BaseLayout>
